# Test: le test attribution report is reachable through le's dispatch and refuses what it cannot judge
# VALIDATES: spec-test-validation-in-smaller-units AC-15 -- the action is
# registered at `le test attribution report`, takes its keywords (log, package,
# tags, repeated file), and refuses with exit 2 and the fix, never an empty
# report that reads as "none caused": a log with no failing test, a package
# pattern, and a missing file keyword. The classification itself is decided by
# TestAttributionClassifiesEachFailingTest with an injected runner; this test
# answers only what a unit test cannot, that the real command line reaches it.
# The logs are repository files: a non-harness le step runs at the checkout
# root (repositoryAnchoredBinary, internal/test/runner/runner.go), so a tmpfs
# file's bare name would not resolve there.
# Exercises: answerReport -> buildRequest -> readFailed (runlog.FailedTests) -> Attributor.Attribute

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test attribution report log internal/le/test/attribution/testdata/passing.log package internal/le/runlog tags ze_core file internal/le/runlog/runlog.go:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=names no failing test
reject=stdout:contains=verdict:

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test attribution report log internal/le/test/attribution/testdata/failing.log package internal/le/... tags ze_core file internal/le/runlog/runlog.go:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=name one package directory, not a pattern

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test attribution report log internal/le/test/attribution/testdata/failing.log package internal/le/runlog tags ze_core:exit=2
expect=stderr:contains=file
expect=exit:code=2
